---
import manageMerge from "../../captures/manage-merge.png";
import mergedEntry from "../../captures/merged-entry.png";
import Callout from "../../guide/Callout.astro";
import GuidePage from "../../guide/GuidePage.astro";
import Path from "../../guide/Path.astro";
import Task from "../../guide/Task.astro";
---

<GuidePage
  slug="merged-entries"
  lead="When a title is published in several places or languages, merge them into one entry with every version inside."
>
  <Task id="merge" title="Merge titles" shot={{ image: mergedEntry, alt: "Pepper&Carrot as one entry holding its English and Japanese editions", caption: "Two editions, one entry" }}>
    <p>Start from wherever the titles are:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>In the library, long-press the titles to select them and tap <strong>Merge</strong>.</li>
      <li>On a title's page, tap <strong>Add to merge</strong> and pick the library entry to merge it into.</li>
      <li>In Browse or a feed, long-press a title and tap <strong>Merge into library...</strong></li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Katari then lists the titles in the order the merged entry will show them. The one marked <strong>Root</strong> is the title the
      others join. Drag them into the order you want and tap <strong>Merge</strong>.
    </p>
    <Callout label="What can merge">
      <p>
        Titles must be in the same profile and of the same kind: all comics, all video, or all books. At most one of them can already
        be a merged entry.
      </p>
    </Callout>
  </Task>

  <Task id="manage" title="Change a merge" shot={{ image: manageMerge, alt: "A merged entry's two editions in order, the first marked Root", caption: "Manage merge" }}>
    <p>
      Open the merged entry and tap <Path>⋮ › Manage merge</Path>. Each title's <strong>⋮</strong> menu has <strong>Set as root</strong>,
      <strong>Remove</strong>, <strong>Remove from library</strong> and <strong>Open</strong>. Tap <strong>Save</strong> to keep the changes.
    </p>
    <p>
      A title that is part of a merge says <strong>This entry is part of a merged entry.</strong> on its own page, with buttons to open the
      merged entry or manage it.
    </p>
    <p>To give the merged entry a name of its own, tap <Path>⋮ › Set display name</Path>.</p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="unmerge" title="Unmerge">
    <p>
      <strong>Unmerge</strong> in <strong>Manage merge</strong> splits the entry back into its titles straight away, without asking.
    </p>
    <p>Removing a merged entry from the library removes all of its titles together.</p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="reading" title="Read a merged entry">
    <ul>
      <li>The chapter list has a header for each title, with its source and chapter count. Tap a header to fold that title away.</li>
      <li>History and Updates name the title a chapter comes from when it differs from the merged entry's name.</li>
      <li>
        The cover shows how many titles it holds. To hide that, turn off <strong>Merged entries</strong> under <strong>Cover badges</strong>
        in the library's display settings.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Task>
</GuidePage>
